  8. Whenever the daily summary is produced, the order count is the number of every order in the list, including store-credit orders. Revenue is the sum of the totals of card orders only, where each total is the items after discount plus shipping. The average order value is revenue divided by the number of card orders, rounded down to a whole rupee. It is ₹0 when there are no card orders that day. For example, ₹1,000 of revenue over 3 card orders shows ₹333.
